Semptify-PI reference browser extension
========================================

This is the second Semptify-PI reference plugin. It is a minimal Chrome/
Firefox Manifest V3 extension that demonstrates the provider-differentiated
direct-capability contract against the Semptify plugin API.

What it does
------------

- Lists approved plugins and connects the example-document-organizer plugin.
- Gets a download capability for a file from Google Drive, Dropbox, or OneDrive.
- Gets an upload capability for a new file from the same providers.
- Reports a completed upload to Core (metadata only — no bytes).

The client logic lives in api-client.mjs and is shared by the popup and by the
Node test runner. The popup (popup.html + popup.mjs + popup.css) is a minimal
UI for manual testing.

Install (developer mode)
------------------------

Chrome / Edge
  1. Open chrome://extensions/.
  2. Enable "Developer mode".
  3. Click "Load unpacked" and select this directory.
  4. Open the extension popup.
  5. Enter a mock Core URL (default http://127.0.0.1:9000) and a session token.
  6. Click Connect.

Firefox
  1. Open about:debugging.
  2. Click "This Firefox" -> "Load Temporary Add-on".
  3. Select manifest.json in this directory.
  4. Open the extension popup and connect.

The default Core URL points to the local mock_core. Point it at a real Core
instance when one exists.

Security notes
--------------

- The popup stores the plugin token in chrome.storage.local, not in the web
  page. Do not commit a real token.
- The extension never sends document bytes to Core; it only calls the
  capability endpoints and then uses the returned URL or direct_request to
  talk directly to the tenant's cloud provider.
- Capability headers such as Authorization: Bearer ... are sensitive. They are
  not logged or persisted beyond the chrome.storage.local token.
